  "notes": "FORMS:\n{示|し} (show, indicate) + {唆|さ} (incite, suggest) = to show indirectly.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nUsed as a noun or with する. Common patterns: 〜を{示唆|しさ}する (to suggest ~), {示唆|しさ}に{富|と}む (rich in suggestions/implications).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {示唆|しさ}に{富|と}む: suggestive, full of implications\n- {示唆|しさ}を{与|あた}える: to give a suggestion\n- {示唆|しさ}を{受|う}ける: to receive a suggestion/hint\n- 〜を{示唆|しさ}する: to suggest, to imply\n\nUSAGE:\n{示唆|しさ} is formal and commonly appears in academic writing, news reports, and business contexts. In everyday conversation, ヒント or {暗示|あんじ} (hint) may be used instead. {示唆|しさ}に{富|と}む is a set expression meaning \"thought-provoking\" or \"full of useful insights.\"",
